data.content:
## What Breaks in .NET 11

In EF Core 11, the **sync-over-async fallback for the Cosmos DB provider is fully removed**. The opt-in configuration (`CosmosOptionsExtension` / `EnableSyncOverAsync()`) you used in .NET 10 no longer exists.

All four of your synchronous calls will throw `InvalidOperationException` at runtime:

| Method | Replacement |
|--------|-------------|
| `.ToList()` | `.ToListAsync()` |
| `.First(...)` | `.FirstAsync(...)` |
| `.Count()` | `.CountAsync()` |
| `.SaveChanges()` | `.SaveChangesAsync()` |

## Required Migration

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key points:**
- There is no workaround or compatibility switch in EF Core 11 — async is the only path for the Cosmos provider.
- `Add()` remains synchronous (it's an in-memory operation on the change tracker), only the query/persist calls need `await`.
- You'll need to propagate `async/await` up through your call chain (controllers, services, etc.).
